What is the output of the following Java program demonstrating exception chaining combined with stack trace suppression?
```java
public class SuppressedVsCauseApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RuntimeException master = new RuntimeException("Master");
        Exception cause = new Exception("Underlying");
        Exception suppressed = new Exception("Extra");
        master.initCause(cause);
        master.addSuppressed(suppressed);
        System.out.print(master.getCause().getMessage() + " | ");
        System.out.print(master.getSuppressed().length + ":");
        System.out.print(master.getSuppressed()[0].getMessage());
    }
}
```
